comments.body:
@xrchz 
> We end up punishing those aspiring for formal guarantees worthy of the name because there's perhaps a wish or hope for the ability to deprecate in an environment where it is in fact not possible.

I don't understand how approaches providing hevm levels of formal guarantees are punished by EOF.  hevm can handle all EOF contracts, so customers refraining from calling out to non-EOF contracts will get the full level of hevm guarantees. So you are down to dealing with (rare?) cases where a customer just has to do that.
